  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1255 PM CDT Mon Sep 14 2026\n\nWednesday and Thursday will bring the best shot at rain in some \ntime, but it's not a washout by any means. The aforementioned upper \nlow over the northern Gulf will move inland and then be absorbed by \nthe mid-level ridge by Thursday. Despite this scenario, some showers \nand storms are expected and coverage should be higher than Monday \nand Tuesday as moisture works further inland. Beyond Thursday, the \nECMWF and GFS are in disagreement on the long term pattern, with \nnotable differences with the development of a large scale trough out \nwest and what may transpire as an inverted trough slides east over \nthe northern Gulf this upcoming weekend. For now, will stick with \nthe NBM, but things could certainly become more active towards the \nweekend if things line up properly.",
